# Audio files (exclude all except TTS outputs)
*.mp3
*.wav
*.zip
# The `!data/completed-tts/**` negations were removed 2026-07-31.
#
# They dated to 2025-09-09 ("exclude all except TTS outputs"), before the
# publishing architecture changed. Since v1.51 finished MP3s are uploaded to
# GitHub Releases and then DELETED locally -- completed-tts/ is a staging area,
# which is exactly what CLAUDE.md says it is.
#
# Keeping them tracked meant every retention run deleted files git still knew
# about, so the working tree carried 7 phantom deletions that nobody committed.
# The deliverable lives in the release assets (verified: daily-2026-07-30 holds
# the day's mp3), so git tracking was duplication that fought retention.

# Jupyter Notebooks
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# Project specific
config/channels.json
config/topics.json
.vercel

# Next.js public/ must NEVER contain a static daily-digest.xml -- it shadows the
# next.config.js rewrite to the dynamic /api/rss/daily-digest route and silently
# freezes the public RSS feed (regressed 2026-06-14, also Oct 2025). Keep the feed
# dynamic-only. (test-feed.xml is a stray test artifact, ignore it too.)
web_ui_hosted/public/daily-digest.xml
web_ui_hosted/public/test-feed.xml

# TypeScript incremental build cache (164K). Rewritten by every `npm run build`,
# which this project requires before every commit -- so tracking it guaranteed a
# permanently dirty working tree. Untracked 2026-07-31.
*.tsbuildinfo
